# sUPI v3.3 TDP — repository exclusions

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Native mechanical CAD — still carries the restrictive marking
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The restrictive-distribution wording lives inside each .prt and .drw file
# (8-9 occurrences per part, 7 in the assembly), not in the shared .frm format,
# so it cannot be cleared with a single template fix. These are binary Creo
# files; they must be corrected in Creo and re-saved, not patched externally.
# They also embed the author name 56-515 times per file.
sUPI Mechanicals/*.prt.1
sUPI Mechanicals/*.drw.1
sUPI Mechanicals/*.asm.1
sUPI Mechanicals/*.frm.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CAD session artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# trail.txt.1 is a Creo session trail containing local Windows user account
# paths, including a corporate cloud-storage path.
sUPI Mechanicals/trail.txt.1
sUPI Mechanicals/*_log.xml

# Altium local history. Contains a nested .git repository, which git cannot
# track as ordinary content, plus every intermediate autosave.
**/.history/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Altium Draftsman source — still carries the restrictive notices
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The .PCBDwf documents are the source of the fabrication and assembly drawing
# PDFs. They still contain the notices that were cleared from the PDFs. The
# format is compressed XML, so the text cannot be edited without Altium.
sUPI Electrical/**/*.PCBDwf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redundant generated output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unpacked ODB++ trees: 147 machine-generated files that duplicate the .tgz
# and .zip archives sitting in the same folder. Archives are tracked.
sUPI Electrical/**/ODB/odb/

# IPC2581 .cvg files are 26-29 MB each and carry the same design data as the
# Gerber and ODB++ sets.
sUPI Electrical/**/IPC2581/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Externally controlled document — not mirrored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Picatinny CLIK Design Standard belongs to another activity and carries its
# own revision history and point of contact. A copy held here goes stale the
# moment they revise it — Table 2 of Rev 3.0 already misstates this package's
# distribution. Consumers should request the current revision from the design
# activity; the README summarises the interface envelope and cites it.
CLIK-Design-Standard-v3.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded source documents
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Converted to Markdown; the .md versions are tracked and carry the
# corrections. Change Log.docx additionally carries the originator's name in
# docProps/core.xml and a Microsoft Purview sensitivity label in
# docMetadata/LabelInfo.xml, neither visible on the page.
sUPI Mechanicals/Change Log.docx
sUPI_Payload_Brief.pdf
sUPI_Platform_Brief.pdf
sUPI Electrical/MFR_*.pdf
MFR_Reference_Design.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .axf: unstripped ELF with a developer username and absolute build paths.
sUPI Firmware/*.axf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal working record
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RELEASE_CHANGES.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
